    "fileId": 6819,
    "type": "Table",
    "diagnosis": "",
    "title": "<p><strong>Table&nbsp;4.05</strong> Surveillance protocol for early tumour detection in <em>TP53</em> mutation carriers {27501770}</p>",
    "legend": "",
    "source": "",
    "copyright": "<p>Villani A, Shore A, Wasserman JD, Stephens D, Kim RH, Druker H, Gallinger B, Naumer A, Kohlmann W, Novokmet A, Tabori U, Tijerin M, Greer ML, Finlay JL, Schiffman JD, Malkin D. Biochemical and imaging surveillance in germline TP53 mutation carriers with Li-Fraumeni syndrome: 11 year follow-up of a prospective observational study. Lancet Oncol. 2016 Sep;17(9):1295-305. Copyright 2016, with permission from Elsevier.</p>",
    "tablehtml": "<table class=\"MsoTableGridLight\" style=\"border-collapse: collapse; border: none;\" border=\"0\" width=\"0\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.0cm; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"227\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Tumour type</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Surveillance strategy</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; border: none; border-top: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #8DB3E2; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>Age range</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"227\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>In children</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Adrenocortical carcinoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Ultrasound of abdomen and pelvis every 3&ndash;4&nbsp;months</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Bloodwork every 3&ndash;4 months:<sup>a</sup>&nbsp;total testosterone, 17-OH-progesterone, DHEAS, androstenedione</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; 24-hour urine cortisol, if feasible</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Birth to 30&nbsp;years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Brain tumour</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Annual MRI of the brain</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Birth to 18&nbsp;years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Soft tissue and bone sarcoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Annual rapid whole-body MRI</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Birth to 18&nbsp;years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Leukaemia/lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Bloodwork every 3&ndash;4&nbsp;months: complete blood count profile, LDH, ESR</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Birth to 18&nbsp;years</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 689.1pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"919\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Complete physical examination every 3&ndash;4&nbsp;months, including anthropometric measurements plotted on a growth curve (with particular attention to rapid acceleration in weight or height), signs of virilization (pubic hair, axillary moisture, adult body odour, androgenic hair loss, clitoromegaly, penile growth), and full neurological assessment</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Prompt evaluation with family physician for any medical concerns</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 6.0cm; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"2\" width=\"227\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>In adults</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" rowspan=\"4\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">Breast cancer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&bull; Monthly breast self-examination</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">From 18&nbsp;years onwards</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&bull; Semiannual clinical breast examination</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">From 20&ndash;25&nbsp;years onwards or from 5&ndash;10&nbsp;years younger than the earliest known breast cancer in the family (whichever comes first)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">&bull; Semiannual breast MRI +/&minus; annual mammography<sup>b</sup></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\" style=\"page-break-after: avoid;\">20&ndash;75&nbsp;years or from 5&ndash;10&nbsp;years younger than the earliest known breast cancer in the family (whichever comes first)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Consider risk-reducing bilateral mastectomy</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Brain tumour</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Annual MRI of the brain</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">From 18&nbsp;years onwards</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Soft tissue and bone sarcoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Annual rapid whole-body MRI</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Ultrasound of abdomen and pelvis every 3&ndash;4&nbsp;months</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">From 18&nbsp;years onwards</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Colorectal cancer</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Biennial colonoscopies</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">From 25&nbsp;years onwards or from 10&nbsp;years younger than the earliest known colon cancer in the family (whichever comes first)</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Melanoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Annual dermatology examination</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">From 18&nbsp;years onwards</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 155.9pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"208\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">Leukaemia/lymphoma</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 276.45pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"369\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Bloodwork every 3&ndash;4&nbsp;months: complete blood count profile, LDH, ESR</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 256.75pt; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"342\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">From 18&nbsp;years onwards</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"page-break-inside: avoid;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" width=\"19\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 689.1pt; border: none; border-bottom: solid windowtext 1.0pt; background: #DAEEF3; padding: 0cm 5.4pt 0cm 5.4pt;\" colspan=\"3\" width=\"919\">\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Complete physical examination every 3&ndash;4 months</p>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\">&bull; Prompt evaluation with family physician for any medical concerns</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p class=\"TableText\"><sup>a</sup>Serial specimens should be obtained at the same time of day and processed in the same laboratory. <sup>b</sup>Breast ultrasonography with mammography as indicated by breast density, but not instead of breast MRI or mammography.</p>",
